&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do quantizations mean?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;4-bit:&lt;/strong&gt; Compresses the model to use less memory. Loses some quality, but it's the most accessible way to run it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;8-bit:&lt;/strong&gt; Good balance between quality and memory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;BF16 (full):&lt;/strong&gt; Maximum quality, requires professional GPU&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule of thumb:&lt;/strong&gt; Your total available memory (RAM + VRAM) should exceed the quantized model size you want to use. If not, it can still run using disk offload, but it won't be ideal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  How to Install It in 2 Minutes
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


  Option 1: Ollama (Easiest)
&lt;/h3&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Install Ollama&lt;/span&gt;
curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-fsSL&lt;/span&gt; ollama.com/install.sh | sh

&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Download and run Gemma 4&lt;/span&gt;
ollama pull gemma4        &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Downloads 26B-A4B by default&lt;/span&gt;
ollama run gemma4         &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Ready to chat&lt;/span&gt;
